#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# re_im_plot

#% text
# `re_im_plot(f, [x, a, b])` plots the real and the imaginary part of f for x from a to b.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is `plot([re(f), im_part(f)], [x, a, b])`, and takes the options of `plot`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A rotating phase:

#% cell
re_im_plot(exp(im*x), [x, 0, 6])
#% output
#= image("re_im_plot.files/re_im_plot-1.svgz")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A function with complex values on part of the line:

#% cell
re_im_plot(sqrt(x), [x, -2, 2])
#% output
#= image("re_im_plot.files/re_im_plot-2.svgz")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# With a legend:

#% cell
re_im_plot((x + im)^2, [x, -2, 2], plot_legends: ["re", "im"])
#% output
#= image("re_im_plot.files/re_im_plot-3.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `abs_arg_plot`, `plot`, `complex_plot`
